  "scope": "# Review \u2014 `3f26d45b9f51`\nTask/source: production v4.0.0, generator SHA-256 `1bd4448f9ff51545858cb402a42521bd7238925667727911e797a8259ee06f5a`.\nGap \u2192 repair: the assigned original ARC family had no small parametric extension; I built an isolated `connection_axes` prototype with `both`, `horizontal`, and `vertical` settings.\nCanonical/reference rule: unchanged; `both` returns the canonical Racket program byte-for-byte and the production generator was not edited.\nResult: selected-task work is routine bounded prototype evidence; it is proposed and unapproved, not a production or training admission.\nFocused checks: 7/7 prototype regressions passed; the final portable selected-task stage passed 23/23 tests.\nRacket evidence: 3 settings \u00d7 (3 demonstrations + 4 queries), with all 21 retained labels executed by the protected Racket runtime.\nIndependent attack: 63 retained setting/output comparisons plus 24 unseen-seed grids passed Python/Racket parity and three-way distinction checks.\nPrivacy attack: public bytes, IDs, manifest coverage, hidden-setting exclusion, and absent query outputs all passed.\nSupplementary tickets: `defba1ab4f90` replay reproduced; `0c2ab7de69d1` has a source-bound teaching-shortcut finding needing maintainer attention.\nRemaining limits: finite prototype coverage, exact-source alternate-program edits, no production battery (not applicable because production behavior is unchanged), and no broader repository suite.\n",
